					<h1 class="title" title="Faizabad Tour">Faizabad Tour</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">

<h3>Location</h3>


<p>Situated on the banks of river <b>Ghaghra, Faizabad</b> also known as the <b>twin city of Ayodhya</b> is 7 km. from 
Ayodhya in the state of <b>Uttar Pradesh</b>. Historians say that Faizabad was present in the days of 
Ramayana where it was known as <b>Saket</b>. Another name by which this city was known in the earlier days 
was <b>'bangla'</b>. There are many places of <b>tourist attractions in Faizabad</b>. </p>

<h3>Places to visit</h3>

<strong>Mausoleum of Shuja-ud Daula-</strong>
<p>There are three important tombs here one belonging to the king, <b>Shuja-ud-daula</b> and the other two of 
his parents. It is considered as one of the <b>important monuments of Faizabad</b>. A large many tourists 
visit this monument every year. Another important monument of historical significance is the <b>Moti Mahal</b>. 
Also known as the <b>Pearl Palace</b>, it represents rich heritage and culture of the Nawabs. With a unique 
identity of its own, it has been recognized as a <b>heritage site of India</b>. Built by Shuja-ud-Daula in 
1764, the <b>Fort Calcutta</b> in Faizabad is a very old fort worth seeing. This was built in order to commemorate 
his defeat in the Buxar battle. Another place to visit is the <b>Botanical Museum</b> at Faizabad. Rare 
specimens of botanical plants can be seen here. </p>

<p>Located at the <b>Guptar Park</b> near the <b>Guptar Ghat</b> is another site of tourist attraction, the 
<b>Faizabad museum</b>. In this museum one can see the historical and mythological displays of the culture 
of the city. The Guptar Park itself is a sight seeing spot and the nearby Guptar Ghat has many temples of 
ancient times. There is a temple known as the <b>Chakra Hajri Vishnu Temple</b> which is famous because it 
is said that the footprints of <b>Lord Rama</b> is present here.  Another botanical garden called the 
Company Gardens is worth visiting. The Gulab Bari which means <b>'the garden of roses'</b> has a great many 
varieties of roses with fountains on all sides. It also has the mausoleum of the second ruler, 
Nawab Shuja-ud-daula. </p>


<p>The military temple which is located in the cantonment area is also a lovely place to visit because of 
its calmness and serenity. There is a tomb which shows a great architectural excellence of those days. 
This is the tomb of the <b>Bahu Begum</b> which is about 42 km. in height and is made out of white marble. 
It is one of the major tourist spot because of its uniqueness and splendor. About 40km. from Faizabad is the 
Shringi Rishi Ashram which is amazing place worth- visiting. Some of the other places of tourist attractions 
are the <b>Raja Mandir</b> and the <b>Ghanta Ghar</b> or the Clock tower located in the heart of the city. </p>



